  "text": "That's a really honest and important realization, Jane. It can feel incredibly limiting when our internal tools don't seem to shift the external reality. It's easy to fall into that trap of thinking, \"If I just processed it better, things would magically change,\" but of course, they won't.\n\nSince journaling is helping you track the feelings even if it doesn't solve the problem yet, have you considered using it to brainstorm *actionable* steps instead? Maybe not about the promotion itself (since that decision is made), but about what you *can* control right now—like updating your resume, reaching out for feedback on why you weren't selected, or exploring other roles within the company? Sometimes shifting focus from \"what happened\" to \"what's next\" can help break that feeling of being stuck.",
